      "writtenOn": "2024-07-03T11:40:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Past experience manually maintaining these finally clauses and debugging/fixing flaky tests has taught us that it\u0027s better to unregister callbacks in tearDown.\n\nA simple way to do this is to define a method on the test class that registers the callback and puts the callback in a list of callbacks to unregister. Then teardown just unregisters all of them. See for example NetworkAgentTest#callbacksToCleanUp . That method will make the code easier to read since it can also encapsulate the runAsShell.\n\nOr you can do something like NetworkCallbackRule - more elegant but may be overkill for just one test.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 876,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 876,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "c1b30986b6b2727f07b37e5d7afc51261dda5865",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
